<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    Nothing, deliberately.

    Android 12 and up always draw a system splash before the app's own, and
    `windowSplashScreenAnimatedIcon` decides what sits in the middle of it.
    Pointing it at the launcher icon meant every launch showed the icon on a
    lavender field, then PINGO's real splash — two splash screens, the first of
    which nobody designed.

    The system splash cannot be skipped, so it is made to disappear instead: a
    transparent icon over the same colour the official artwork starts with. What
    the user sees is one continuous splash that resolves into the real one.
-->
<shape xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android" android:shape="rectangle">
    <solid android:color="@android:color/transparent" />
</shape>
